# bench/results/_cuda69/profile_prefill_1_counters_retained.log
#
# ARM A of the counters A/B.
# Re-measured 2026-08-07 (Mouse, issue #69 revision) after Morpheus's tier ruling.
#
# Why this run exists
# -------------------
# The revision claimed the large undecomposed region inside the Compute callback was the
# benchmark harness's own counters-file dump, not any EP phase. That claim was originally
# supported only by a before/after across two different EP builds, which confounds the
# build change with the counters change. This run isolates the variable.
#
# It was re-measured (not re-reduced) because the earlier generation predates the
# `vulkan.bind_check` span and the tier arguments, and the whole point of the arm is to
# show which tier the moving time lands in. A stored trace with no bind-check spans
# cannot answer that under any reduction.
#
# Single variable: ONNXRUNTIME_EP_VULKAN_BENCH_KEEP_COUNTERS=1.
# Everything else is held: the same release DLL, the same workload (prefill_1), the same
# machine, the same iteration counts, minutes apart from ARM B.
#
#   $env:ONNXRUNTIME_VULKAN_EP_LIB                 = "<worktree>/rust/target/release/onnxruntime_vulkan_ep.dll"
#   $env:ONNXRUNTIME_EP_VULKAN_BENCH_CUDA_PYTHON   = "<worktree>/.venv-cu12/Scripts/python.exe"
#   $env:ONNXRUNTIME_EP_VULKAN_BENCH_KEEP_COUNTERS = "1"
#   .venv-cu12/Scripts/python.exe -m bench.cuda_profile \
#       --workload prefill_1 --iters 10 --skip-cuda \
#       --out bench/results/_cuda69/scratch_ab/profile_counters_on_v4.json \
#       --scratch bench/results/_cuda69/scratch_ab/on_v4
#
# `--skip-cuda`: this arm is a within-EP ablation. Re-running the CUDA reference would
# add a third process to a comparison that is already careful about which process each
# number came from.
#
# The record was copied to this name unmodified. Its `traced_record.trace_path` points
# into the gitignored scratch_ab/ directory (per-worker logs, ORT profiles, counters
# dumps, the Chrome trace this report reduces).
#
# The tier decomposition (traced-run warm-call medians, ms)
# --------------------------------------------------------
#   tier 0  vulkan.compute_call            76.660   <- the bucketing anchor
#   tier 1    vulkan.bind_check             0.129
#   tier 1    vulkan.subgraph              38.259   <- the dispatch region
#   tier 1    unattributed_in_call         36.392   <- the counters dump lands here
#   tier 2      record+submit+fence_wait   27.490
#   tier 2      unattributed_in_subgraph    9.654
#
# Result of the A/B (ARM A here, ARM B in profile_prefill_1.log)
# --------------------------------------------------------------
#   term                        ARM A (this)   ARM B (first_run_only)
#   unattributed_in_call_ms         36.392             0.016
#   bind_check_ms                    0.129             0.035
#   subgraph_ms                     38.259            31.092
#   compute_call_ms                 76.660            31.163
#   traced median                   78.816            31.526
#   untraced median                 71.028            30.316
#   gpu_ms_per_run                  20.179            19.002
#
# `unattributed_in_call_ms` moves 36.4 ms; `bind_check_ms` moves 0.09 ms. The dump lands
# after `dispatch_ort` returns -- exactly where the tier-0 anchor sees it and the tier-1
# dispatch region does not. That is the whole finding.
#
# What this does NOT show
# -----------------------
# It does not attribute the region to bind checking. `bind_check` is measured separately,
# is two orders of magnitude smaller, and barely moves. The withdrawn claim that a bind
# check explains ~23 ms is refuted by this pair of runs, not merely deleted.
#
# It also does not rank optimisation candidates. Each arm's numbers are within-process;
# nothing is subtracted across the two processes, and no per-candidate ablation was run.
#
# ORT cross-check on this arm: ORT fused node 77.745 ms vs anchor 76.660 ms (+1.4% on
# ORT's side), within one process. The counters dump inflates ORT's own fused-node
# measurement too, which is what an in-callback cost should do.
#
# verdict: GPU_TIME_MEASURED, refusals: []